item.description:
arXiv:2611.01518v2 Announce Type: replace 
Abstract: In this paper, we focus on well-filtered spaces. By using the Rudin sets and WD sets, we obtain the following results:
  (1) The product of arbitrarily many Scott well-filtered dcpos is still well-filtered with respect to the Scott topology. Thus we give positive answers for two questions proposed by Xu and Zhao;
  (2) Let $P$ be a dcpo with $\Sigma K(P)$ being well-filtered and $Q$ an RB-domain. Then $\Sigma K(P\times Q)$ is well-filtered if $K(P\times Q)$ is a dcpo;
  (3) An intrinsic characterization of the $WD$ sets is given in terms of Scott open filters.
